    "result_text": "The full build is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nConsolidated the three separate owner duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived **`identityKey`** and reject a create with 409 only on a whole-key match.\n\n**identityKey** = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId` \u2014 because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household with different telephones produce different keys and are both allowed; only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.\n\n### Changes\n\n- **New `OwnerIdentityKey`** \u2014 the single source of the key, `of(telephone, email, householdId)` and `of(Owner)`, with `null` components rendered as empty strings.\n- **New `OwnerHousehold`** \u2014 extracted the household-membership/derivation logic (previously duplicated inside `AssignOwnerHousehold` and `CheckUniqueOwnerHousehold`) into one place. Its `resolve(request, repo)` returns the householdId a request *would* be assigned, so the key computed at check-time matches the one stored and returned.\n- **New `CheckUniqueOwnerIdentity`** \u2014 the one pipeline check: builds the new owner's key (resolving its prospective householdId) and rejects with `DuplicateIdentityException` (\u2192 409) when it equals any existing owner's key. Placed where the old checks were (before `build`), so 409 keeps priority over the city/daily-limit rules.\n- **New `DuplicateIdentityException` + handler + escalation YAML** \u2014 responds 409 with `{\"errors\":[\"identityKey\"]}`.\n- **`AssignOwnerHousehold`** \u2014 rewritten to use `OwnerHousehold`, guaranteeing the stored householdId matches the one the check used.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 three check steps (`checkUniqueEmail`, `checkUnique`, `checkHousehold`) replaced by one `checkIdentity`.\n- **`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` field to the `Owner` schema and derive it in the mapper, so it's **returned** on both create and read responses.\n- **Deleted** the three old check functions, their three exceptions + handlers, and their three escalation YAMLs.\n\nVerified `coreRejectsIdentityCollision` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The old behaviour (any-of telephone/email/household match \u2192 409) is now the intended narrower rule: only a full identityKey collision is a duplicate.",
